{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531857-questions-about-changeling","id":1531857,"title":"Questions about Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-02T15:48:39-08:00","id":1531857,"title":"Questions about Changeling","content":"My group is about to start a new Changeling game. We have all played before back in second edition in the 90s, but none of us have played recently or played the current edition. So far we have made characters and skimmed the 20th anniversary book, but I still have a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1: Do changelings have to do anything special to see chimerical reality / the dreaming or is it just something they can do with their normal senses?<br /> <br /> 2: Can changelings enter the dreaming bodily without using a freehold / trod?<br /> <br /> 3: Can reweaving change the physical form of a living creature? The text says no, but the examples say yes.<br /> <br /> 4: Are characters bound by the letter of an oath, or the spirit?<br /> <br /> 5: Is there any limitation on how many oaths can be made? What stops someone with Contracts 5 from just endlessly creating trivial oaths as a source of infinite willpower, glamour, and an endless banality sink?<br /> <br /> 6: Do bystanders play along with the new reality created by reweaving? Do mortals and prodigals react differently? Does the subject play along with their new identity?<br /> <br /> 7: One of the characters has a Lightning Gun. Does it inflict the -2 dice penalty on its target in the same manner as the Lord of Levin cantrip? If not, what is the point of it? A 5 dot treasure that is no more effective than an ordinary gun but with a bunch of requirements to use?<br /> <br /> 8: Speaking of Lord of Levin, I notice that in the printed book it does aggravated damage and in the .pdf it does lethal damage. Is this an errata thing? If so, which one takes precedence? And does anyone have a list of the other changes between the physical and digital rulebooks?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T23:58:33-08:00","id":1531867,"title":"","content":"Is it possible you have the kickstarter pre-release pdf? The final kickstarter pdf for example does list Lord of Levin doing agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T12:27:09-07:00","id":1535793,"title":"","content":"1- Changelings see the Chimerical Reality constantly, as long as they're not taken by the Mists, with no penalty or extra effort. They see both realities with no problem; <br /> 2- Without a Trod they need a specific power, although the correct Art isn't particularly rare, nor the power is too high level;<br /> <br /> 3- Don't remember and don't have my book available now;<br /> <br /> 4- Whichever the Dream deems the right answer at the moment, basically ST's decision with no obligation to be coherent about it. Changelings do know that the distinction is unreliable at best;<br /> <br /> 5- Again, the Dreaming. There's no limit, but anyone abusing the power of Oaths and Contracts is playing with fire and may be hit by the Dreaming itself making creative interpretations;<br /> <br /> 6- Again, not with the book, though I distinctly remember Naming being quite powerful;<br /> <br /> 7- Probably, treasures usually have the full effect of a Cantrip, their limitations are only on how to use, not what they do;<br /> <br /> 8- Fire deals Agg, I think there's no reason to expect less from this Cantrip. Agg sources aren't really rare in WoD in general.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T06:33:55-07:00","id":1537483,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info! Sorry I didn\u2019t see this until now, I had given up hope waiting for a reply!<br /> <br /> The oath questions are pretty disappointing, I play at a table of rules lawyers who have vert little trust in each other or the Storyteller, and trying to use trickery and GM FIAT to police oaths is, while very appropriate to the genre, not going to fly at my table!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T09:22:03-07:00","id":1537494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531857-questions-about-changeling?p=1537483#post1537483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the info! Sorry I didn\u2019t see this until now, I had given up hope waiting for a reply!<br /> <br /> The oath questions are pretty disappointing, I play at a table of rules lawyers who have vert little trust in each other or the Storyteller, and trying to use trickery and GM FIAT to police oaths is, while very appropriate to the genre, not going to fly at my table!</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, in CtD the Dreaming is kind of an active agent by itself. Changelings know this, so they're in-character aware of how unreliable that is.<br /> <br /> If you really want to make a rule, roll a die, 6 or more the Dreaming goes along with the plan.<br /> <br /> You can improvise a whole system of rolls where the player rolls a number of dice depending on how they justify their actions (add Contract to the pool <b><u>if</u></b> the Art is involved), and the difficulty depends on how much they're stretching things (number of active Oaths would be a good general measure).<br /> <br /> But the problem with a harder rule than that is that it would actually rob your players (and NPCs) of options. As is, the players know they have a chance at not being screwed when they think out-of-the-box, one way or another, while abuse don't need to be dealt with unless it becomes a big problem (and then it is dealt with swiftly). They also exert more caution without trying to game the numbers.<br /> <br /> Make it always the letter, and you'll turn Oaths into landmines better suited to a game of Demon than Changeling. Make it always the spirit and you make Oaths too conveniently ironclad, and basically kill the usefulness of high-level Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}